step Rough Blasting Powder to 35
  tip Rough Blasting Powder is orange at 1 (yellow 20, green 30, grey 40): about 46 crafts to 35. Each takes 1 Rough Stone. One Rough Stone a craft; Rough Stone comes with the Copper Ore from Copper Veins.
  craft 3918 until 35

step Engineering recipes at 35
  tip Back to an Engineering trainer: Handful of Copper Bolts (from 30, 1s 15c). Also learn Reagent Bot (1s): Forever's Engineering camp item, placed at a campsite beside a campfire. It takes a Handful of Copper Bolts and a Copper Tube, which you learn at 30 and 50, so it gives no points. The Camping 101: Engineering quest from your starting area's camping guide (after The Great Outdoors) sends you to an engineering trainer who teaches it free.
  learn 3922
  learn 1230656

step Handful of Copper Bolts to 57
  tip Handful of Copper Bolts is orange at 35 (yellow 45, green 52, grey 60): about 33 crafts to 57. Each takes 1 Copper Bar. One Copper Bar a craft. Keep the bolts: Practice Locks and later gadgets take them. Needs an anvil nearby. Blacksmith Hammer is a tool: keep it in your bags.
  craft 3922 until 57

step Engineering recipes at 57
  tip Back to an Engineering trainer: Arclight Spanner (from 50, 1s 50c) and Copper Tube (from 50, 1s 50c).
  learn 7430
  learn 3924

step Copper Tube to 75
  tip Copper Tube is orange at 57 (yellow 80, green 95, grey 110): about 18 crafts to 75, a point every craft. Each takes 2 Copper Bar and 1 Weak Flux. Two Copper Bars and a Weak Flux a craft (blacksmithing and engineering suppliers). Needs an anvil nearby. Make the Arclight Spanner now, while it still gives a point: a later recipe needs it in your bags, so keep it there.
  craft 7430 x1 -- a tool: keep it in your bags
  craft 3924 until 75
  skill Engineering 75

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Journeyman (75-150)
section Engineering 75-150

step Journeyman Engineering
  tip Journeyman raises the cap from 75 to 150 for 5s (Classic's price; Forever's is not in the data); it needs Engineering 50 and character level 10, so you can take it on any visit from 50. Not every Engineering trainer teaches it: Alliance Finbus Geargrind (Duskwood), Lilliam Sparkspindle (Stormwind City) and Trixie Quikswitch (Ironforge); Horde Franklin Lloyd (Undercity). The arrow picks the nearest of your faction. Learn now: Coarse Blasting Powder (from 75, 2s 50c) and Crafted Heavy Shot (from 75, 2s 50c). 75-150 takes about 5s of recipes and 45s of vendor goods, plus 15 Coarse Stone, 27 Heavy Stone, 72 Copper Bar, 61 Bronze Bar and 2 Silver Bar to gather or buy.
  level 10
  train Engineering Journeyman
  learn 3929
  learn 3930

step Engineering 75-150: vendor goods
  tip Buy the whole bracket's share in one go: 45 Weak Flux (45s); about 45s in all. The arrow picks the nearest seller of your faction (Stormwind City: Billibub Cogspinner, Brooke Stonebraid and Edna Mullby).
  buy 2880 x45 nearest

