step Crafted Heavy Shot to 94
  tip Crafted Heavy Shot is orange at 75 (yellow 85, green 90, grey 95): about 15 crafts to 94. Each takes 1 Coarse Blasting Powder and 1 Copper Bar and makes 200. Make the 15 Coarse Blasting Powder first: it gives points too while not grey. The Coarse Blasting Powder in each gives its own point while it is not grey: two chances a craft. Sell the shot to hunters or a vendor.
  craft 3929 x15
  craft 3930 until 94

step Copper Tube to 100
  tip Copper Tube is yellow at 94 (yellow 80, green 95, grey 110): about 14 crafts to 100. Each takes 2 Copper Bar and 1 Weak Flux. Two Copper Bars and a Weak Flux a craft (blacksmithing and engineering suppliers). Needs an anvil nearby. If you got here without learning Copper Tube, learn it now: an earlier step teaches it.
  learn 3924
  craft 3924 until 100

step Engineering recipes at 100
  tip Back to an Engineering trainer: Practice Lock (from 100).
  learn 8334

step Practice Lock to 125
  tip Practice Lock is orange at 100 (yellow 115, green 122, grey 130): about 31 crafts to 125. Each takes 1 Bronze Bar, 2 Handful of Copper Bolts and 1 Weak Flux. Make the 29 Handful of Copper Bolts first. Use the 33 Handful of Copper Bolts you made earlier; the counts above leave them out. Practice Locks sell to rogues, or open them yourself. Needs an anvil nearby. If you got here without learning Handful of Copper Bolts, learn it now: an earlier step teaches it.
  learn 3922
  craft 3922 x29
  craft 8334 until 125

step Engineering recipes at 125
  tip Back to an Engineering trainer: Heavy Blasting Powder (from 125).
  learn 3945

step Heavy Blasting Powder to 140
  tip Heavy Blasting Powder is yellow at 125 (yellow 125, green 135, grey 145): about 27 crafts to 140. Each takes 1 Heavy Stone. One Heavy Stone a craft (Iron Deposits). Keep some: Iron Grenades take one each.
  craft 3945 until 140

step Engineering recipes at 140
  tip Back to an Engineering trainer: Silver Contact (from 90) and Big Bronze Bomb (from 140).
  learn 3973
  learn 3950

step Big Bronze Bomb to 150
  tip Big Bronze Bomb is yellow at 140 (yellow 140, green 165, grey 190): about 10 crafts to 150. Each takes 2 Heavy Blasting Powder, 3 Bronze Bar and 1 Silver Contact and makes 3. Make the 10 Silver Contact (2 crafts) first. Use the 20 Heavy Blasting Powder you made earlier; the counts above leave them out. The trainer teaches it, and it is the cheapest way through these points in the data. Needs an anvil nearby. Engineering 150 is a Legacy System milestone.
  craft 3973 x2
  craft 3950 until 150
  skill Engineering 150

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Expert (150-225)
section Engineering 150-225

step Expert Engineering
  tip Expert raises the cap from 150 to 225 for 50s (Classic's price; Forever's is not in the data); it needs Engineering 125 and character level 20, so you can take it on any visit from 125. Only a few trainers teach it: Alliance Springspindle Fizzlegear (Ironforge); Horde Roxxik (Orgrimmar). The arrow picks the nearest of your faction. Learn now: Aquadynamic Fish Attractor (from 150) and Bronze Framework (from 145). 150-225 takes about 31s of vendor goods, plus 19 Medium Leather, 19 Wool Cloth, 31 Coarse Stone, 74 Heavy Stone, 100 Bronze Bar, 6 Silver Bar, 81 Iron Bar, 19 Mithril Bar and 62 Solid Stone to gather or buy.
  level 20
  train Engineering Expert
  learn 9271
  learn 3953

step Engineering 150-225: vendor goods
  tip Buy the whole bracket's share in one go: 31 Nightcrawlers (31s); about 31s in all. The arrow picks the nearest seller of your faction (Stormwind City: Catherine Leland and Edna Mullby).
  buy 6530 x31 nearest

step Get Medium Leather (Alliance)
  only Alliance
  zone Hillsbrad Foothills
  tip You need 19 Medium Leather for Engineering 150-225: Bronze Framework. Skinning: beasts of level 18-30. Skin Cave Yeti, Elder Gray Bear, Feral Mountain Lion, Gray Bear, Snapjaw, Starving Mountain Lion and Vicious Gray Bear here (level 18-30); the Skinning guide routes this. Or buy them at the Auction House.
  collect 2319 x19 @41,34.5 era gather Skinning 80
  auction 2319 x19

step Get Medium Leather (Horde)
  only Horde
  zone Ashenvale
  tip You need 19 Medium Leather for Engineering 150-225: Bronze Framework. Skinning: beasts of level 18-30. Skin Ashenvale Bear, Elder Ashenvale Bear, Elder Shadowhorn Stag, Ghostpaw Runner, Giant Ashenvale Bear and Shadowhorn Stag here (level 18-30); the Skinning guide routes this. Or buy them at the Auction House.
  collect 2319 x19 @68.7,50.2 era gather Skinning 80
  auction 2319 x19

step Get Wool Cloth
  zone Azeroth
  tip You need 19 Wool Cloth for Engineering 150-225: Bronze Framework. Humanoids of level 15-30 drop it, and what you loot as you level counts. The arrow takes you to the best farm for your level: mobs at or below it first, then the most Wool Cloth per minute and the nearest; it picks again as you level. The guide window shows the kills and minutes it takes there and a second choice. Or buy them at the Auction House.
  collect 2592 x19 nearest gather levels 15-30
  auction 2592 x19

step Get Coarse Stone
  tip You need 31 Coarse Stone for Engineering 150-225: Aquadynamic Fish Attractor. Mining: Tin Vein (skill 65) in Ashenvale (18-30), Hillsbrad Foothills (20-30) and Wetlands (20-30). The arrow takes the Mining loop that gets you them soonest from where you are and walks it until your bags hold them; the window names the loop, its lap and the laps left. Or buy them at the Auction House.
