step Aquadynamic Fish Attractor to 166
  tip Aquadynamic Fish Attractor is yellow at 150 (yellow 150, green 160, grey 170): about 31 crafts to 166. Each takes 2 Bronze Bar, 1 Nightcrawlers and 1 Coarse Blasting Powder and makes 3. Make the 31 Coarse Blasting Powder first. Nightcrawlers come from trade and fishing suppliers; the attractors sell to fishermen. If you got here without learning Coarse Blasting Powder, learn it now: an earlier step teaches it.
  learn 3929
  craft 3929 x31
  craft 9271 until 166

step Bronze Framework to 175
  tip Bronze Framework is yellow at 166 (yellow 145, green 170, grey 195): about 19 crafts to 175. Each takes 2 Bronze Bar, 1 Medium Leather and 1 Wool Cloth. Bronze Frameworks are parts for later gadgets; the extras sell to vendors.
  craft 3953 until 175

step Engineering recipes at 175
  tip Back to an Engineering trainer: Solid Blasting Powder (from 175).
  learn 12585

step Solid Blasting Powder to 191
  tip Solid Blasting Powder is yellow at 175 (yellow 175, green 185, grey 195): about 31 crafts to 191. Each takes 2 Solid Stone. Two Solid Stone a craft (Mithril Deposits). Make plenty: the triggers, slugs and Gyro-Shot all use it.
  craft 12585 until 191

step Engineering recipes at 191
  tip Back to an Engineering trainer: Big Iron Bomb (from 190).
  learn 3967

step Big Iron Bomb to 210
  tip Big Iron Bomb is yellow at 191 (yellow 190, green 210, grey 230): about 27 crafts to 210. Each takes 3 Iron Bar, 3 Heavy Blasting Powder and 1 Silver Contact and makes 2. Make the 74 Heavy Blasting Powder and 30 Silver Contact (6 crafts) first. Use the 7 Heavy Blasting Powder you made earlier; the counts above leave them out. A Silver Bar makes five Silver Contacts (grey by now: no points, but no trip to a vendor either); the Heavy Blasting Powder comes from Heavy Stone. Each craft makes two bombs. Specialisation (optional): at 200 and character level 30, Springspindle Fizzlegear (Ironforge), Lilliam Sparkspindle (Stormwind), Graham Van Talen (Undercity) or Tinkerwiz (Ratchet) sends you to Gnomish Engineering (Tinkmaster Overspark, Ironforge, or Oglethorpe Obnoticus, Booty Bay: 6 Mithril Tubes, an Accurate Scope and 2 Advanced Target Dummies) or Goblin Engineering (Nixx Sprocketspring, Gadgetzan: 20 Big Iron Bombs, 20 Solid Dynamite and 5 Explosive Sheep). The Accurate Scope schematic now binds when picked up, but the quest takes a scope someone else made. The membership card lasts 14 days of play; renewing it costs 2g. You can take only one; neither is needed for 300, and the beta never tested them (it stopped at level 30). Needs an anvil nearby. If you got here without learning Heavy Blasting Powder and Silver Contact, learn them now: an earlier step teaches them.
  learn 3945
  learn 3973
  craft 3945 x74
  craft 3973 x6
  craft 3967 until 210

step Engineering recipes at 210
  tip Back to an Engineering trainer: Hi-Impact Mithril Slugs (from 210).
  learn 12596

step Hi-Impact Mithril Slugs to 225
  tip Hi-Impact Mithril Slugs is yellow at 210 (yellow 210, green 230, grey 250): about 19 crafts to 225. Each takes 1 Mithril Bar and 1 Solid Blasting Powder and makes 200. Use the 19 Solid Blasting Powder you made earlier; the counts above leave them out. One Mithril Bar and one Solid Blasting Powder a craft; hunters buy the slugs. Needs an anvil nearby. Engineering 225 is a Legacy System milestone.
  craft 12596 until 225
  skill Engineering 225

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Artisan (225-300)
section Engineering 225-300

step Artisan Engineering
  tip Artisan raises the cap from 225 to 300 for 4g 50s (Classic's price; Forever's is not in the data); it needs Engineering 200 and character level 35, so you can take it on any visit from 200. Only a few trainers teach it: Alliance Buzzek Bracketswing (Tanaris); Horde Buzzek Bracketswing (Tanaris). The arrow picks the nearest of your faction. 225-300 takes about 2g 80s of recipes, plus 118 Mithril Bar, 212 Solid Stone, 156 Thorium Bar and 24 Runecloth to gather or buy.
  level 35
  train Engineering Artisan

step Schematic: Thorium Widget
  tip Schematic: Thorium Widget teaches Thorium Widget (Engineering 260) for 1g 20s. Sold by Alliance: Gearcutter Cogspinner (Ironforge), limited stock; Horde: Sovik (Orgrimmar), limited stock. Its sellers keep one or two in stock that come back some time after a sale; the Auction House often has it too.
  buy 16042 nearest

step Schematic: Thorium Tube
  tip Schematic: Thorium Tube teaches Thorium Tube (Engineering 275) for 1g 60s. Sold by Kor'gar (Riverglades) and Xizzer Fizzbolt (Winterspring), limited stock.
  buy 16047 nearest

step Get Mithril Bar
  tip You need 118 Mithril Bar for Engineering 225-300: Hi-Impact Mithril Slugs and Mithril Gyro-Shot. Mine Mithril Ore and smelt it at a forge (Mining 175). The arrow takes the Mining loop that gets you them soonest from where you are and walks it until your bags hold them; the window names the loop, its lap and the laps left. Or buy them at the Auction House.
